  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {肩|かた}をすくめる: to shrug one's shoulders (the most common usage)\n- {首|くび}をすくめる: to draw in one's neck, to duck one's head\n\nPAIR: すくめる（{他動詞|たどうし}）↔ すくむ（{自動詞|じどうし}）= to freeze, to cower\n\nUSAGE: Almost always appears with {肩|かた}を or {首|くび}を as the object. The gesture of shrugging shoulders is less natural in Japanese culture, so this expression often appears in translated literature or when describing Western-style gestures.",
